# Thai Basil Beef and Lemongrass Rice Bowls

**Source:** https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/20-minute-thai-basil-beef-lemongrass-rice-bowls/
**Serves:** 4 | **Time:** About 20 minutes for the beef and salad (the rice takes longer, see notes)

## Ingredients

### Lemongrass Rice
- 1 can coconut milk
- 1/3 cup water
- 1 1/2 cups jasmine rice
- 1 tablespoon lemongrass paste

### Salad
- 1 cup shredded carrots
- 1 bell pepper, sliced
- 1/2 cup cherry tomatoes, halved
- 2 green onions, chopped
- 2 tablespoons toasted sesame oil
- 2 tablespoons lime juice
- 1 tablespoon rice vinegar
- 1 tablespoon fish sauce or tamari
- 2 teaspoons honey

### Beef
- 1 pound lean ground beef (or chicken or pork)
- 4 cloves garlic, chopped
- 1 tablespoon fresh grated ginger
- Black pepper
- 1/3 cup tamari or soy sauce
- 1/3 cup sweet Thai chili sauce (store-bought or homemade, see notes)
- 2 cups Thai or Italian basil, chopped, divided
- Sesame seeds and peanuts, for topping

## Steps

### Rice (start this first)
1. Bring the coconut milk and water to a gentle boil in a medium pot.
2. Stir in the rice and lemongrass paste, cover, and turn the heat to the lowest setting. Cook 10 minutes.
3. Turn off the heat and let it steam, covered, for 15–20 minutes. Don't lift the lid.
4. Fluff with a fork.

### Salad
1. Toss all the salad ingredients together in a bowl and set aside.

### Beef
1. Brown the beef with some black pepper in a large skillet over medium heat, breaking it up as it cooks, about 5 minutes.
2. Add the garlic and ginger and cook 1 minute more.
3. Stir in the tamari, chili sauce, and 1 cup of the basil. Simmer 3–5 minutes, until the sauce clings to the meat.
4. Take off the heat and stir in the rest of the basil.

### To Serve
1. Divide rice and beef among bowls, add plenty of salad, and top with peanuts, sesame seeds, and extra basil.

## Notes
- **Timing:** the "20 minutes" doesn't include the rice's cooking and steaming time, so start the rice before anything else.
- **Homemade sweet Thai chili sauce:** shake together 1/3 cup honey, 2 Tbsp ketchup, 1–2 Tbsp chili sauce, 2 tsp lime zest, 2 Tbsp lime juice, 1 Tbsp rice vinegar, 2 tsp tamari or soy sauce, 1 Tbsp grated ginger, and 1 grated garlic clove in a jar.
- **Swaps:** chicken, pork, or tofu instead of beef; Italian basil instead of Thai.
- **Reader tips:** some found it too salty or saucy. Try low-sodium tamari or simmer the sauce a bit longer.
